;
; BASIC-DOS Primes Demo: module definitions for LINK4, which builds PRIMES.EXE
; as an NE program whose stub is the MS-DOS program that LINK builds (see the
; TESTS makefile).  PROTMODE marks the NE program as protected-mode only, and
; FIXED segments make its relocations refer to segment numbers (instead of
; entry table ordinals).
;
; @author Jeff Parsons <Jeff@pcjs.org>
; @copyright (c) 2026 Jeff Parsons
; @license MIT <https://basicdos.com/LICENSE.txt>
;
; This file is part of PCjs, a computer emulation software project at pcjs.org
;
NAME	PRIMES
STUB	'OBJ\PRIMES.EXE'
PROTMODE
CODE	FIXED
DATA	FIXED
